From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Songjun Li <lisongjun@radxa.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:28:11 +0800
Subject: i2c: qcom-geni: Fix standalone reads in GPI mode

The multi_msg flag is initialized to false and is not updated before
preparing the TX channel configuration when the first message is a
read. As a result, the GPI driver encodes the GO TRE as a write instead
of a read.

This affects the Raspberry Pi 7-inch touchscreen ATTINY driver, which
writes a register address and performs a separate read after a delay.
The firmware ID check sees 0x00 and the device fails to probe.

Set multi_msg according to the current message's I2C_M_RD flag before
preparing the channel configuration, ensuring that transfers starting
with a read generate the correct READ GO TRE.

Fixes: 83ef106fa732 ("i2c: qcom-geni: Correct I2C TRE sequence")
Signed-off-by: Songjun Li <lisongjun@radxa.com>
Reviewed-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
(cherry picked from commit a4f7d514f4b3ed6b1239e817dcf765cd1c6257e2)
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
@@ -912,8 +912,7 @@ static int geni_i2c_gpi_xfer(struct geni_i2c_dev *gi2c, struct i2c_msg msgs[], i
 			peripheral.stretch = 1;
 
 		peripheral.addr = msgs[i].addr;
-		if (i > 0 && (!(msgs[i].flags & I2C_M_RD)))
-			peripheral.multi_msg = false;
+		peripheral.multi_msg = !!(msgs[i].flags & I2C_M_RD);
 
 		ret =  geni_i2c_gpi(gi2c, msgs, &config,
 				    &tx_addr, &tx_buf, I2C_WRITE, gi2c->tx_c);
-- 
Armbian

